From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team <oe.patch@openatv.example>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GLES2: define format enums missing from legacy STB headers

Some vendor GLES2 header sets used by STBs predate the GL_RED, GL_RG and
GL_R16F enum definitions. Kodi 22's generic GL format helpers reference these
values even when compiled for GLES2. The R16F upload already has a GLES2
luminance fallback when the driver rejects the format. Keep the compatibility
definitions in the central GL include wrapper so all GLES users see the same
guarded values without pretending that the runtime supports GLES3.

diff --git a/xbmc/system_gl.h b/xbmc/system_gl.h
--- a/xbmc/system_gl.h
+++ b/xbmc/system_gl.h
@@ -41,3 +41,15 @@
 #endif
 #endif
 #endif
+
+#ifdef HAS_GLES
+#ifndef GL_RED
+#define GL_RED 0x1903
+#endif
+#ifndef GL_RG
+#define GL_RG 0x8227
+#endif
+#ifndef GL_R16F
+#define GL_R16F 0x822D
+#endif
+#endif
